==Secondary holidays==
Secondary holidays are typically religious in nature, and thus are not recognized at the confederal level.
* '''[[W:Fat Tuesday|Fat Tuesday]]''', The day of [[W:Carnival|Carnival]]. Known as ''[[Dijous Gras]]'' in [[Estuaria]]. 
* '''[[W:Ash Wednesday|Ash Wednesday]]''' Wednesday after Carnival, the last Carnival day.
* '''[[W:Good Friday|Good Friday]]''', the Friday preceding [[W:Easter Sunday|Easter Sunday]], is a communal holiday in many places.
* [[W:Christmas|'''Christmas''']], celebrated December 25th.
* [[W:Eid al-Fitr|'''Eid al-Fitr''']], marks the end of the month-long dawn-to-dusk fasting of [[W:Ramadan|Ramadan]].
* [[W:Diwali|'''Diwali''']], the five-day celebration is observed every year sometime from the second half of October to the first half of November coinciding with a new moon (''[[W:Amāvasyā|amāvasyā]]'') as per the [[W:Hindu calendar|Hindu lunisolar calendar]].
* [[W:Holi|'''Holi''']], a Hindu festival marking the end of winter, arrival of spring, and the blossoming of love.
* [[W:420 (cannabis culture)|'''4/20''']], cannabis-oriented celebrations that take place annually on 20 April (4/20 in Illypnian date form) with observers [[W:Smoke-in|gathering in public to smoke]]. Due to confederal recognition of the [[Cosmopolitan Church of Cannabis]] (CCC), it is considered by some to be a "religious" holiday.

==Regional holidays==
Confederal initiatives recognize the right of all territories to commemorate holidays. Some of the more notable ones are:
* February 22: Founding of ''Guardafui'', [[Castejón]] only.
* July 6: [[Carpinchera Republic|Republic Day]], [[Carpinchera]] only.

